WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.060 --> 00:00:04.960
A trailer for the final season of Game of
Thrones is out.

00:00:04.960 --> 00:00:09.709
And it shows that the start of Season 8 is
a lot like the start of Season 1 – with

00:00:09.709 --> 00:00:12.730
a queen and a king coming to Winterfell.

00:00:12.730 --> 00:00:17.480
But this time, the queen is Daenerys, and
the king is Jon Snow.

00:00:17.480 --> 00:00:23.359
Daenerys brings her army of Unsullied, and
a boy watches from above, just like how Bran

00:00:23.359 --> 00:00:25.810
watched from above in Episode 1.

00:00:25.810 --> 00:00:31.019
Daenerys also brings her dragons – the first
dragons at Winterfell in a over a hundred

00:00:31.019 --> 00:00:32.019
years.

00:00:32.019 --> 00:00:39.200
There’s a lotta magic and symbolism in these
creatures of fire flying above this icy fortress.

00:00:39.200 --> 00:00:43.140
Sansa Stark has never seen dragons and magic
before.

00:00:43.140 --> 00:00:47.600
Most of her story has been in the south with
the political plots, so she was uncomfortable

00:00:47.600 --> 00:00:51.630
last season, with psychic Bran and Faceless
Arya.

00:00:51.630 --> 00:00:57.140
If Season 8 is all about fantastical magical
battles – how will Sansa and her skills

00:00:57.140 --> 00:00:58.350
fit in?

00:00:58.350 --> 00:01:04.869
Sansa has enjoyed ruling Winterfell – will
Queen Daenerys threaten her power?

00:01:04.869 --> 00:01:08.330
Arya also sees her first dragon – and she’s
excited.

00:01:08.330 --> 00:01:13.429
She’s always wanted adventure and freedom
and power – and that’s what dragons represent

00:01:13.429 --> 00:01:19.100
. Arya is a fan of Visenya Targaryen , a dragon
queen from hundreds of years ago.

00:01:19.100 --> 00:01:23.430
So maybe Arya will also like Daenerys, this
new dragon queen.

00:01:23.430 --> 00:01:28.560
We see Jon and Daenerys with the dragons,
Rhaegal and Drogon – Rhaegal is the green

00:01:28.560 --> 00:01:30.860
one, and Drogon the red one.

00:01:30.860 --> 00:01:35.189
Daenerys rides Drogon – it’s named after
her first husband, Drogo.

00:01:35.189 --> 00:01:37.500
And Rhaegal is named after Rhaegar Targaryen.

00:01:37.500 --> 00:01:40.799
Rhaegar is Daenerys’ brother, and Jon’s
real father.

00:01:40.799 --> 00:01:42.860
So maybe Jon will ride Rhaegal.

00:01:42.860 --> 00:01:47.640
There could be a cute montage of Daenerys
teaching Jon to ride – oh wait we already

00:01:47.640 --> 00:01:48.829
saw that.

00:01:48.829 --> 00:01:53.520
The dragons have a bunch of blackened bones
– which was probably their breakfast.

00:01:53.520 --> 00:01:57.200
But we heard least season that Winterfell
doesn’t have enough food for its people

00:01:57.200 --> 00:02:01.139
– so will they be able to feed two giant
dragons?

00:02:01.139 --> 00:02:07.490
If they get too hungry, they might start eating
people, which was a problem in Meereen.

00:02:07.490 --> 00:02:12.700
Daenerys used to have three dragons – but
Viserion was killed and taken by the Night

00:02:12.700 --> 00:02:13.700
King.

00:02:13.700 --> 00:02:17.760
Can Drogon and Rhaegal defeat their undead
sibling?

00:02:17.760 --> 00:02:20.180
Jon stands in the Winterfell godswood.

00:02:20.180 --> 00:02:23.580
This is where Ned Stark came to pray and contemplate.

00:02:23.580 --> 00:02:26.110
Jon thinks that Ned is his father.

00:02:26.110 --> 00:02:31.330
But last season, Bran and Sam learned the
truth – that Jon is the son of Rhaegar and

00:02:31.330 --> 00:02:36.180
Lyanna . Sam plans to tell Jon about his parents
, and he looks worried.

00:02:36.180 --> 00:02:41.560
Cause the truth will make Jon and Dany’s
relationship a lot more complicated .For one

00:02:41.560 --> 00:02:45.201
thing, it means that Daenerys is Jon’s aunt
– and they boatsexed.

00:02:45.201 --> 00:02:51.400
But also, Daenerys’ identity is built on
her being “the last Targaryen” , heir

00:02:51.400 --> 00:02:52.579
to the Throne.

00:02:52.579 --> 00:02:58.049
If Jon is the true heir, ahead of Daenerys
– what has Dany been fighting for all this

00:02:58.049 --> 00:02:59.049
time?

00:02:59.049 --> 00:03:05.659
It also questions Jon’s identity – is
he a Stark or a Targaryen, a bastard or a

00:03:05.659 --> 00:03:06.659
king?

00:03:06.659 --> 00:03:11.150
It looks like Jon and Dany have a D&amp;M in the
Winterfell crypts, possibly by the statue

00:03:11.150 --> 00:03:13.500
of Jon’s real mother, Lyanna.

00:03:13.500 --> 00:03:18.870
This again parallels Episode 1, when Ned and
Robert discuss Lyanna in the crypts.

00:03:18.870 --> 00:03:24.230
We also see Tyrion, who was very concerned
last season about Jon and Dany’s relationship.

00:03:24.230 --> 00:03:27.220
How will he react to Jon’s true parentage?

00:03:27.220 --> 00:03:30.129
And whose side is Tyrion really on?

00:03:30.129 --> 00:03:35.769
There might not be time to angst over incest
– because the white walkers are coming to

00:03:35.769 --> 00:03:41.790
attack Winterfell . Jaime Lannister arrives,
and says he’ll help “fight for the living”

00:03:41.790 --> 00:03:46.129
. Last season, Jaime promised to help fight
the white walkers , and now, he wants to keep

00:03:46.129 --> 00:03:47.420
that pledge.

00:03:47.420 --> 00:03:52.909
Jaime has always been hated as an oathbreaker
and kingslayer – this war is Jaime’s chance

00:03:52.909 --> 00:03:53.930
at redemption.

00:03:53.930 --> 00:03:59.370
He’s got a lot of crimes to redeem – last
time he was at Winterfell, Jaime crippled

00:03:59.370 --> 00:04:00.370
Bran.

00:04:00.370 --> 00:04:03.620
Jaime fought Ned, and warred against Robb.

00:04:03.620 --> 00:04:06.939
Will the Starks make alliance with their enemy?

00:04:06.939 --> 00:04:07.939
Probably.

00:04:07.939 --> 00:04:12.870
Because as Jon says, everyone alive is “on
the same side” now – fighting against

00:04:12.870 --> 00:04:14.080
the dead.

00:04:14.080 --> 00:04:16.769
So everyone prepares for battle at Winterfell.

00:04:16.769 --> 00:04:21.989
We see Davos on the walls – even though
he isn’t much of a fighter . We see Edd,

00:04:21.989 --> 00:04:23.180
Tormund and Beric.

00:04:23.180 --> 00:04:28.120
It looked like Beric and Tormund mighta died
last season when the Wall fell – but they’ve

00:04:28.120 --> 00:04:29.770
survived to fight again.

00:04:29.770 --> 00:04:33.570
Edd became commander of the Night’s Watch
when Jon left – now looks like he musta

00:04:33.570 --> 00:04:35.520
ran south when the Wall fell.

00:04:35.520 --> 00:04:42.780
But how much of the Night’s Watch survived?

00:04:42.780 --> 00:04:47.060
Maybe with the white walkers coming, everyone
is Night’s Watch now.

00:04:47.060 --> 00:04:52.130
We see Gendry with a big pile of dragonglass,
mined from Dragonstone – Gendry’ll need

00:04:52.130 --> 00:04:54.639
to make a bunch of weapons to fight the dead.

00:04:54.639 --> 00:04:59.370
But hopefully there’ll also be time for
him to reunite with his old friend Arya.

00:04:59.370 --> 00:05:01.419
We see Jorah and the Dothraki.

00:05:01.419 --> 00:05:03.770
Jorah has the sword Heartsbane.

00:05:03.770 --> 00:05:08.139
This is the Valyrian sword of House Tarly
that Sam took from his dad.

00:05:08.139 --> 00:05:12.430
But Sam isn’t good with a sword, so it makes
sense he’d give Heartsbane to Jorah – they

00:05:12.430 --> 00:05:16.470
made friends last season.

00:05:16.470 --> 00:05:20.520
We see Brienne and Podrick with the knights
of the Vale – these guys only came north

00:05:20.520 --> 00:05:24.290
to help fight the Boltons, they never signed
up for this World War Z shit.

00:05:24.290 --> 00:05:27.890
But again, everyone’s coming together to
fight the dead.

00:05:27.890 --> 00:05:32.440
We see Grey Worm kiss Missandei – while
Jon’s voiceover says that the white walkers

00:05:32.440 --> 00:05:36.630
don’t feel . This is a reminder of why everyone’s
fighting.

00:05:36.630 --> 00:05:43.020
This war isn’t for a lord or a throne – this
is about the survival of life and love itself

00:05:43.020 --> 00:05:46.120
against the cold dead enemy.

00:05:46.120 --> 00:05:49.520
Grey Worm looks intense as he prepares for
battle.

00:05:49.520 --> 00:05:53.940
The Unsullied were bred to be emotionless
, but with Missandei, Grey Worm has found

00:05:53.940 --> 00:05:58.819
a something worth fighting for . There are
trebuchets behind the Unsullied, maybe to

00:05:58.819 --> 00:06:01.039
throw fire at the dead.

00:06:01.039 --> 00:06:06.379
While the warriors prepare for battle, we
see women and children and Varys in the crypts.

00:06:06.379 --> 00:06:10.740
This is like the battle of Helm’s Deep in
Lord of the Rings – a Game of Thrones director

00:06:10.740 --> 00:06:16.229
said he studied that battle for this episode
. Varys looks scared and out of place, when

00:06:16.229 --> 00:06:20.880
he used to be so confident and powerful in
the politics of King’s Landing.

00:06:20.880 --> 00:06:25.900
How can Varys stay relevant in this magical
apocalyptic finale?

00:06:25.900 --> 00:06:30.240
We should, at least, get some good conversations
here during the battle – it could be like

00:06:30.240 --> 00:06:33.639
in the Red Keep during the battle of the Blackwater.

00:06:33.639 --> 00:06:36.650
In the background, we see Gilly and her baby.

00:06:36.650 --> 00:06:41.311
Remember, this baby was originally meant to
be sacrificed to the white walkers, and when

00:06:41.311 --> 00:06:46.620
Gilly took the baby south instead, the walkers
came after him . It’s possible that the

00:06:46.620 --> 00:06:49.129
walkers still want Gilly’s baby.

00:06:49.129 --> 00:06:53.880
It’s also possible that the dead might rise
from these crypts – there are hints in the

00:06:53.880 --> 00:06:59.259
books about ancient Starks with white walker
blood, go watch that video.

00:06:59.259 --> 00:07:01.150
The battle for Winterfell begins.

00:07:01.150 --> 00:07:04.270
Brienne and Jaime fight the dead on the walls.

00:07:04.270 --> 00:07:09.129
Brienne wields the Valyrian sword Oathkeeper,
while Jaime uses Widow’s Wail.

00:07:09.129 --> 00:07:12.340
Both these swords were made from the Stark
sword Ice.

00:07:12.340 --> 00:07:17.640
So the reunion of Brienne and Jaime has all
sorts of symbolic weight to it.

00:07:17.640 --> 00:07:23.120
This is also kinda like a dream Jaime has
in the books, where he and Brienne wield flaming

00:07:23.120 --> 00:07:28.159
swords, and face the dead amidst darkness
and doom . Which connects to the prophecy

00:07:28.159 --> 00:07:34.850
of Azor Ahai, and Nissa Nissa, and maybe the
deaths of Jaime and Brienne.

00:07:34.850 --> 00:07:37.300
We see the Hound amidst fire.

00:07:37.300 --> 00:07:41.789
And the Hound is afraid of fire, because when
he was young, his brother the Mountain burned

00:07:41.789 --> 00:07:43.210
his face.

00:07:43.210 --> 00:07:49.120
Fire is why the Hound ran from battle in Season
2, and was afraid of Beric in Season 3.

00:07:49.120 --> 00:07:55.060
Maybe now, the Hound will face his fear to
defeat the dead who haunt him – both metaphorically

00:07:55.060 --> 00:07:56.180
and literally.

00:07:56.180 --> 00:08:00.840
Cause it’s hinted that the Hound will face
the Mountain in a fight called Cleganebowl.

00:08:00.840 --> 00:08:05.610
Since the Mountain is undead, the Hound might
need fire to defeat him.

00:08:05.610 --> 00:08:11.710
We also see Jon running, doing something heroic
– in the books, he also has a dream of fighting

00:08:11.710 --> 00:08:13.380
the dead with fire.

00:08:13.380 --> 00:08:17.590
We see horses running across snow, and it
looks like there might be some wolves in there

00:08:17.590 --> 00:08:18.590
as well.

00:08:18.590 --> 00:08:25.479
We might see Jon’s direwolf Ghost, or even
the wolf pack led by Arya’s direwolf, Nymeria.

00:08:25.479 --> 00:08:31.440
We see Arya doing some spin moves with a stick
– like the Faceless Men trained her.

00:08:31.440 --> 00:08:34.740
Or maybe it’s a dragonglass spear to kill
the dead.

00:08:34.740 --> 00:08:40.039
But her victim here has a lot of blood – zombies
don’t usually bleed that much.

00:08:40.039 --> 00:08:45.170
Remember, the white walkers can also raise
animals, like polar bears, and there are stories

00:08:45.170 --> 00:08:52.200
of giant ice spiders . The night is dark and
full of terrors, and Arya may face them.

00:08:52.200 --> 00:08:54.589
Arya says “I know Death.

00:08:54.589 --> 00:08:55.760
He's got many faces.

00:08:55.760 --> 00:09:00.910
I look forward to seeing this one” . Cause
remember, the Faceless Men taught Arya about

00:09:00.910 --> 00:09:04.170
the Many-Faced God, a name for Death.

00:09:04.170 --> 00:09:09.440
The Night King, leader of the white walkers,
is an embodiment of death – a symbol of

00:09:09.440 --> 00:09:14.030
the people Arya’s killed, and maybe of her
own death.

00:09:14.030 --> 00:09:19.709
Arya takes a dragonglass dagger, to kill white
walkers, but it looks like things go badly

00:09:19.709 --> 00:09:20.769
for her.

00:09:20.769 --> 00:09:26.050
The trailer starts with Arya looking scared
and hurt in the dark – she’s got a wound

00:09:26.050 --> 00:09:29.030
on her head, and she’s running in terror.

00:09:29.030 --> 00:09:31.579
When was the last time Arya looked so scared?

00:09:31.579 --> 00:09:36.690
It looks like Arya is running from zombies,
but why’s she so afraid if she’s a dragonglass

00:09:36.690 --> 00:09:39.200
dagger and Valyrian blade?

00:09:39.200 --> 00:09:42.290
Maybe those zombies were people she knew.

00:09:42.290 --> 00:09:47.050
Maybe they’re dead Starks risen from the
crypts, her mother or her brother.

00:09:47.050 --> 00:09:51.120
One way or another, it looks like death is
catching up with Arya.

00:09:51.120 --> 00:09:55.810
In Book 1, Jon jokes that Arya will die in
the winter – that they’ll find her body

00:09:55.810 --> 00:09:59.839
with a needle still locked tight between her
fingers .

00:09:59.839 --> 00:10:05.360
So at Winterfell, almost every character is
desperately fighting for the survival of all

00:10:05.360 --> 00:10:06.360
life.

00:10:06.360 --> 00:10:09.860
But down in King’s Landing, Cersei is scheming
to save herself.

00:10:09.860 --> 00:10:14.170
She’s got a shiny new outfit, looking smug
and powerful – and she’s with her two

00:10:14.170 --> 00:10:18.810
best friends, the creepy mad scientist Qyburn,
and the zombie Mountain.

00:10:18.810 --> 00:10:24.670
Most everyone else has died or abandoned her,
including Jaime.

00:10:24.670 --> 00:10:30.180
Last season, Cersei sent Euron Greyjoy to
buy a mercenary group called the Golden Company.

00:10:30.180 --> 00:10:34.990
Here they’re on Euron’s ships, with their
leader “Homeless” Harry Strickland.

00:10:34.990 --> 00:10:39.570
The Golden Company is said to be “the most
powerful army in Essos”, with twenty thousand

00:10:39.570 --> 00:10:45.100
men, horses, and elephants . So we finally
gonna get some oliphont action in Game of

00:10:45.100 --> 00:10:46.180
Thrones.

00:10:46.180 --> 00:10:50.740
In the books, the Golden Company has a complex
plotline involving the Blackfyres, and a kid

00:10:50.740 --> 00:10:52.339
called Young Griff.

00:10:52.339 --> 00:10:55.930
None of that seems to be happening in the
show – the Company is just here to help

00:10:55.930 --> 00:11:00.149
Cersei cling to the Throne until the bitter
end.

00:11:00.149 --> 00:11:04.589
This looks like Strickland standing before
Cersei on the Throne, with the Mountain and

00:11:04.589 --> 00:11:10.970
Qyburn, but this character is unclear – maybe
Euron, or the banker Tycho Nestoris, or even

00:11:10.970 --> 00:11:13.110
Sansa with the red hair?

00:11:13.110 --> 00:11:15.060
It’s hard to tell.

00:11:15.060 --> 00:11:19.200
In this shot, Cersei looks more vulnerable
– she’s got sort of a smile, but also

00:11:19.200 --> 00:11:20.700
tears in her eyes.

00:11:20.700 --> 00:11:25.730
She’s drinking wine, which is weird, cause
last season, Cersei said she was pregnant.

00:11:25.730 --> 00:11:31.120
Maybe Cersei loses her unborn child – and
with nothing left to protect, she’ll unleash

00:11:31.120 --> 00:11:33.720
her full fury upon Westeros.

00:11:33.720 --> 00:11:36.420
There also this weird shot.

00:11:36.420 --> 00:11:40.760
Maybe it’s Jon at Winterfell – or maybe
it’s Arya in King’s Landing – that could

00:11:40.760 --> 00:11:43.210
be a brazier in the Great Hall.

00:11:43.210 --> 00:11:47.480
It looks she’s holding a bow, and we know
Arya can use a bow.

00:11:47.480 --> 00:11:52.640
Maybe this shot is Arya is trying to kill
Cersei, like she said she would last season

00:11:52.640 --> 00:11:57.100
. Will Arya kill the queen?

00:11:57.100 --> 00:12:01.350
There are rumours that this’ll be the only
trailer for Season 8 – so this might be

00:12:01.350 --> 00:12:04.420
the last ever trailer for Game of Thrones.

00:12:04.420 --> 00:12:09.350
We’re gonna make the most of the final season
– so make sure you subscribe and click the

00:12:09.350 --> 00:12:10.389
bell.

00:12:10.389 --> 00:12:14.180
Analysing a new Game of Thrones trailer is
like solving a puzzle.

00:12:14.180 --> 00:12:18.860
You gotta find connections between bits of
information, to find an explanation that makes

00:12:18.860 --> 00:12:19.940
sense.

00:12:19.940 --> 00:12:24.720
